KNOWNBUG
assignment-to-increasing-range-bit1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.v\[0\] == 1\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(##1 main\.v == 128\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The RTL construction maps a constant bit-select on the left-hand side
to a bit position without taking the direction of the range into
account: for a vector declared with an increasing range [0:7], v[0]
must denote the most significant bit (1800-2017 7.4.1), but the
assignment writes the least significant bit. The read of v[0] in the
property is lowered correctly, and hence p0 is refuted.
